==English==

===Etymology===
* From {{etyl|la}} ''[[refractum]]'', the neutralal inflection of [[refractus]], the past participle of [[refringere]], itself from re- 'again' + [[frangere]] 'to break'.

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{context|intransitive|of light}} To change [[direction]] as a result of entering a different [[medium]]
# {{transitive}} (''Optics'') To cause (light) to change direction as a result of entering a different medium.
#: ''A prism can '''refract''' light.''

